Verdict: **ACCEPT_WITH_LIMITATIONS** (dissent preserved in STATE.json).

## Known limitations (honest)
1. Rapier 0.19.3 KCC clips box corners ~0.8m on diagonal approaches
   (measured; head-on face contact holds ≤0.05m). Tolerance documented as
   -0.9m. Upgrade path: Rapier ≥ 0.20 (also restores `computedSlopeAngle`).
2. Ground collision is a flat 200×200 cuboid (matches the rendered flat
   GroundPlane; the settlement model has no heightmap). `addTerrainHeightfield`
   is ready for the first heightmap source.
3. `running` stays true after Esc — stepping is frozen via the playtestMode
   gate (verified frozen), pause() is not called.
4. ACCEPTANCE_PASSED on the maturity ladder awaits the formal
   failure-injection suite (dynamic WASM-failure exercise); the failure path
   is code-verified and visibly surfaces via the DOM HUD.
5. Engine-runtime command path does not own the physics world (future work).
